---
import SabGuide from '../../components/sab/SabGuide.astro';
import { getGuide } from '../../lib/guides';

const guide = getGuide('scholarships-for-lethbridge-students');

const faqJson = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  'mainEntity': [
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      'name': 'What scholarships are available for Lethbridge students?',
      'acceptedAnswer': {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        'text': 'Local awards include those from the two post-secondary institutions in the city, with the University of Lethbridge running four separate awards and Lethbridge Polytechnic reaching more than 400 awards worth over $800,000 through a single application.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      'name': 'Which Lethbridge scholarships do I need to start preparing for early?',
      'acceptedAnswer': {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        'text': 'Two. The Health Care Professionals of Tomorrow Scholarship requires you to be a registered AHS volunteer at Chinook Regional Hospital with at least 40 lifetime hours, which cannot be accumulated in your graduating spring, so start in Grade 10 or 11. The Aspiring Artist Award is open from Grade 9 but runs on nominations, so you must ask an art teacher or someone in the local arts community to put you forward.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      'name': 'How do I get the University of Lethbridge Board of Governors Award?',
      'acceptedAnswer': {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        'text': 'Grade 12 students applying to ULethbridge are automatically considered, with no separate application. It pays $1,000 and runs off the December 15 early admission deadline, which is the earliest date in the Lethbridge cycle.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      'name': 'Are there University of Lethbridge scholarships for Grade 11 students?',
      'acceptedAnswer': {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        'text': 'Yes. The Grade 11 Merit Award pays $800 off a 75% average and is submitted before June 30 of your Grade 11 year. By Grade 12 it has closed for you, and the Board of Governors Award is the one to aim at.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      'name': 'What is the best return for a single application in Lethbridge?',
      'acceptedAnswer': {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        'text': 'The Lethbridge Polytechnic form. One application reaches more than 400 awards worth over $800,000, and the same form is how Alberta residents apply for the Jason Lang and Louise McKinney provincial scholarships.',
      },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Question',
      'name': 'Are the Lethbridge County Community Benefit Scholarship and the Stirling Wind Project scholarship the same award?',
      'acceptedAnswer': {
        '@type': 'Answer',
        'text': 'Yes. The county runs it with the Stirling Wind Project and some lists name it the Stirling Wind Project Community Benefit Scholarship, so do not apply twice thinking they are separate. It gives two $2,000 awards to students entering a STEM program, closing June 1.',
      },
    },
  ],
};
---

<SabGuide guide={guide}>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqJson)} slot="ld" />

  <p>
    Lethbridge students can apply through the city’s two post-secondary institutions, schools and community organisations. Some awards require volunteer hours or a nomination, so check those requirements early. The <a href="/scholarships/lethbridge/">Lethbridge directory</a> has the current local listings.
  </p>

  <h2>After graduation: the Rutherford</h2>
  <p>
    Once enrolled in post-secondary, apply for the <a href="/guides/alexander-rutherford-scholarship-guide/">Alexander Rutherford Scholarship</a>. It pays up to $2,500 for qualifying high school marks and can be combined with local awards.
  </p>

  <h2>The two awards to start early</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/scholarships/health-care-professionals-of-tomorrow-scholarship/">Health Care Professionals of Tomorrow Scholarship</a> is the one to find early. Two of its four awards are reserved for graduating Grade 12 students, at $4,000 for first place and $3,000 for second, but you must be a registered AHS volunteer at Chinook Regional Hospital with at least 40 lifetime hours. The hours have to be at that hospital, so they cannot be earned in your graduating spring. Start in Grade 10 or 11. Health care is defined broadly here and is not limited to direct patient care roles. Applications are due at noon, not end of day.
  </p>
  <p>
    The <a href="/scholarships/aspiring-artist-award/">Aspiring Artist Award</a> is open from Grade 9, but it runs on nominations rather than applications. You cannot put yourself forward. If you make art seriously, the action item is to ask an art teacher or someone in the local arts community to nominate you, and to ask well before the deadline.
  </p>

  <h2>The University of Lethbridge</h2>
  <p>
    Four separate awards, each with its own date. Grade 12 students applying to ULethbridge are automatically considered for the <a href="/scholarships/university-of-lethbridge-board-of-governors-award/">Board of Governors Award</a> at $1,000 with no separate application, and it runs off the December 15 early admission deadline, which is the earliest date on this page. Grade 11 students have their own route: the <a href="/scholarships/university-of-lethbridge-grade-11-merit-award/">Grade 11 Merit Award</a> pays $800 off a 75% average, submitted before June 30 of your Grade 11 year. Do not wait until Grade 12 to notice it, because by then you are looking at the Board of Governors award instead.
  </p>
  <p>
    Above those sit the <a href="/scholarships/university-of-lethbridge-chinook-scholarship/">Chinook Scholarship</a> at $5,000, which wants an 85% average, a reference letter, and full-time enrolment across both fall and spring, and the <a href="/scholarships/university-of-lethbridge-high-school-entrance-awards/">High School Entrance Awards</a> worth up to $6,000, which are a pool of named scholarships with different criteria. Some weigh marks, others leadership, financial need, or artistic ability, and you apply through the Bridge student portal.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are heading to <a href="/scholarships/lethbridge-polytechnic-entrance-award/">Lethbridge Polytechnic</a> instead, one application reaches more than 400 awards worth over $800,000, and the same form is how Alberta residents apply for the Jason Lang and Louise McKinney provincial scholarships.
  </p>

  <h2>County and community awards</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/scholarships/lethbridge-county-community-benefit-scholarship/">Lethbridge County Community Benefit Scholarship</a> gives two $2,000 awards to students entering a STEM program, closing June 1. The county runs it with the Stirling Wind Project and some lists name it the Stirling Wind Project Community Benefit Scholarship, so do not apply twice thinking they are separate awards. The <a href="/scholarships/lethbridge-county-bursary-program/">Lethbridge County Bursary Program</a> is listed at three $1,500 bursaries with financial need in the selection, but the county only advertises the Community Benefit Scholarship, so this may be the same award under an older name. Contact the County before applying to both.
  </p>
  <p>
    The <a href="/scholarships/lethbridge-school-division-ice-scholarship/">Lethbridge School Division ICE Scholarship</a> rewards innovation, creativity and entrepreneurship for a division student who shows initiative and original problem-solving. Its 2026 window ran January 13 to April 29 and the division had not posted 2027 dates when this was checked, so the dates shown are last year's.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Lethbridge and District Pro-Life Association runs two Grade 12 awards, the <a href="/scholarships/elsie-alexander-essay-scholarship/">Elsie Alexander Essay Scholarship</a> at $1,000 and the <a href="/scholarships/elsie-alexander-work-and-volunteer-scholarship/">Work and Volunteer Scholarship</a> at $500, and you can apply for both in the same year: one is decided on a written submission, the other on service. Their catchment runs north to Nanton and Vulcan, east to the Saskatchewan border, and south and west to the United States and British Columbia borders. The 2026 cycle has closed and no 2027 date was posted when this was checked, so there is nothing to plan against yet; the association announces reopening through its newsletter.
  </p>

  <h2>Arts and culture</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/scholarships/ray-jolliffe-memorial-scholarship/">Ray Jolliffe Memorial Scholarship</a> is worth $3,000 and is a behind-the-scenes theatre award: the eligible programs are production design and management, or media production and design, rather than performance. The Allied Arts Council lists March 31 without tying it to a year, which suggests a fixed annual date. The <a href="/scholarships/mac-nishiyama-memorial-scholarship/">Mac Nishiyama Memorial Scholarship</a> is $500 from the Nikkei Cultural Society, but the society's two pages disagree on who can apply: the awards page says any southern Alberta high school graduate, while the about page describes it as being for students interested in Japanese language or culture. There is no published deadline or form, so email info@nikkeiculturalsociety.com and ask which applies before you spend time on it.
  </p>

  <h2>Working the Lethbridge list</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Put December 15 in your calendar now.</strong> The ULethbridge early admission deadline carries the Board of Governors award with it, months ahead of everything else here.</li>
    <li><strong>If healthcare is the plan, start volunteer hours this year.</strong> Forty lifetime hours at Chinook Regional Hospital cannot be backfilled in your final spring.</li>
    <li><strong>One Polytechnic form reaches 400 awards.</strong> Fill it even if you are unsure, because it also carries Jason Lang and Louise McKinney.</li>
    <li><strong>Apply to everything you plausibly qualify for.</strong> <a href="/guides/local-scholarships-better-odds/">Local awards</a> draw from one county or one school, not the whole country.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Several dates on this page are last year's, because the providers had not posted new ones when we checked. Treat them as a planning guide and confirm before you rely on one. <a href="/match/">Build my combo</a> sorts the Lethbridge list by what you qualify for.
  </p>
</SabGuide>
